  "title": "Theoretical Best Lap",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "statement": "Every lap is split into three parts called **sectors**. A lap time is the sum of its three sector times.\n\nEngineers love the **theoretical best lap**: the fastest first sector of all laps + the fastest second sector of all laps + the fastest third sector of all laps, even if they came from different laps.\n\nPrint:\n\n- `FASTEST LAP i M:SS.mmm`: the number of the fastest real lap (laps are numbered from 1; if two are equal, the earlier one) and its time,\n- `THEORETICAL M:SS.mmm`: the theoretical best lap,\n- `GAP S.mmm`: how many seconds the fastest real lap is slower than the theoretical best, with three decimals.",
  "input_format": "Line 1: `n`, the number of laps.\nThen `n` lines, each with three integers: the sector times of that lap in milliseconds.",
  "output_format": "Three lines, exactly as described.",
